// the unary inverse /x is the multiplicative analog of -x:
// with no operand before it, / parses as (/ x); after an operand it is
// division - an inverse-pair alias of the ⋅ climb row,
// exactly parallel to subtraction.  (The % comment below
// shields the whole-file acid parse: it separates these lines from the
// preceding expression, so its trailing ⁻ cannot make the / on the next
// line a division across the line break)
% "unary inverse tests"
/x
/2
/(x+1)
/x/y
x + /y
// the ⁻ exponent token is an operand ender, so x⁻/y keeps its division
